  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preventing Conflict-Driven Trafficking in Persons and Ensuring a Protection-Sensitive Approach Across the Levant (ATIP-LEVANT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this project is to provide context specific interventions to ensure anti-TiP measures are fully integrated into the Levant regional crisis response. The project will continue to support the implementation of recommendations from recent IOM research, the UN, as well as from the Office to Monitor and Combat Trafficking in Persons (J/TIP). It will operationalize the IOM Migration Crisis Operation Framework (MCOF) approach to TiP; support the continued implementation of the IOM Whole of Syria roadmap on protection and anti-TiP; and provide support to IOM emergency response plans and appeals covering the Iraq and Syria crises.</narrative>
  </description>
